{
  "company_name": "WindPeak Energy",
  "industry": "Power Generation",
  "use_case": "Wind farm performance optimization and turbine health monitoring",
  "space_title": "WindPeak Energy - Wind Farm Optimization \ud83d\udca8",
  "space_description": "**Subindustry:** Power Generation\n\n**Use case:** Wind Farm Performance & Turbine Health Optimization\n\nWindPeak Energy \u2014 wind farm operations analytics across 20 turbines and multiple farms. Turbine Engineers and Plant Managers use this space to monitor capacity factor, power-curve deviation, and vibration; the Trading desk and CFO use it to track PPA revenue, curtailment exposure, and forecast accuracy against day-ahead commitments.\n\n**Key KPIs**\n- Capacity factor (%) \u2014 onshore wind benchmark ~35%, offshore ~45%\n- Turbine availability (%) \u2014 IEC 61400-26 target >97%\n- Power curve deviation (%) \u2014 degradation or wake-loss indicator\n- Wake loss (%) \u2014 typical 5-15% across a wind farm\n- Wind speed (m/s) \u2014 primary dispatch driver; cut-in ~3 m/s, rated ~12 m/s\n- Curtailment (MWh) \u2014 grid-imposed losses\n- Forecast accuracy \u2014 PPA settlement risk\n- Vibration level (g) \u2014 leading indicator of gearbox/bearing failure\n\n**Data sources**\n- `wind_turbines` \u2014 daily generation, capacity factor, wind speed, status per turbine\n- `performance_readings` \u2014 power-curve deviation, wake loss, blade pitch, rotor RPM, vibration\n- `wind_snapshots` \u2014 forecasted vs actual MWh, curtailment, revenue, PPA price, availability",
  "schema_basename": "wind_optimization",
  "tables": [
    {
      "table_name": "wind_turbines",
