  "genie_instructions": "DOMAIN CONTEXT\nThis space supports wind farm optimization and turbine health monitoring across 20 turbines. Personas: Turbine Engineer (power_curve_deviation_pct, wake_loss_pct, vibration_level_g, rotor_rpm), Plant Manager (capacity_factor_pct, generation_mwh, turbine_status, availability_pct), Trading desk (forecasted_generation_mwh vs actual, curtailment_mwh, revenue_usd, ppa_price_mwh), and CFO (revenue settlement, curtailment exposure).\n\nMETRIC DEFINITIONS\n- Capacity factor = capacity_factor_pct; onshore benchmark ~35% (US new builds 40-45%), offshore ~45-50%.\n- Turbine availability = availability_pct; IEC 61400-26 target >97%.\n- Power curve deviation = power_curve_deviation_pct; sustained >5% indicates pitch issue or blade soiling.\n- Wake loss = wake_loss_pct; typical 5-15% farm-wide; >20% may justify control optimization.\n- Wind speed = avg_wind_speed_ms; cut-in ~3 m/s, rated ~12 m/s, cut-out ~25 m/s.\n- Vibration = vibration_level_g; ISO 10816-21 thresholds; >0.7g sustained triggers inspection.\n- Forecast accuracy ~ actual_mwh / forecasted_mwh; PPA settlement target \u00b110%.\n- Curtailment = curtailment_mwh; multiply by ppa_price_mwh for revenue impact.\n\nQUERY GUIDANCE\n- ALWAYS prefer metric views with MEASURE() syntax for aggregations.\n  - turbine_kpi_monthly (source: wind_turbines) \u2014 dims: record_date, turbine_model, wind_farm, turbine_status; measures: total_generation_mwh, avg_capacity_factor, avg_wind_speed, generating_count, total_turbine_count, max_generation_mwh.\n  - wind_forecast_monthly (source: wind_snapshots) \u2014 dims: snapshot_date, wind_farm; measures: total_forecasted_mwh, total_actual_mwh, total_curtailment_mwh, total_revenue, avg_availability, total_ppa_price_mwh, unique_turbine_count, max_forecasted_generation_mwh.\n- Use GROUP BY ALL with MEASURE() queries.\n- For monthly trends, always wrap the date in DATE_TRUNC('month', <date_col>).\n- For \"Top X\" requests, return LIMIT 10 unless the user specifies otherwise.\n- Query base tables directly only when needing columns not exposed by metric views (e.g. turbine_id, turbine_name, power_curve_deviation_pct, wake_loss_pct, vibration_level_g, ppa_price_mwh).\n- When the user's phrasing matches a SQL snippet display name (filters, expressions, or measures), prefer that snippet.",
  "sample_questions": [
    "Show monthly total wind generation MWh by wind farm for the trailing 12 months.",
    "Top 10 turbines by average capacity factor over the last 90 days.",
    "Which wind farms had the largest gap between forecasted and actual MWh this quarter?",
    "How has total curtailment MWh trended month-over-month, and what is the implied revenue loss?",
    "Which turbines show sustained power curve deviation above 5% or vibration above 0.7g this year?",
    "Top 10 wind farms by total revenue USD year-to-date \u2014 and how does that compare to last year?",
    "What is the monthly trend in average wind speed across all turbines, by farm?"
  ],
  "example_sqls": [
    {
      "question": "How does peak energy generated in mwh compare across turbines?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT record_date, MEASURE(max_generation_mwh) AS max_generation_mwh",
        "FROM {fqn}.turbine_kpi_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY record_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has total energy generated in mwh trended over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT record_date, MEASURE(total_generation_mwh) AS total_generation_mwh",
        "FROM {fqn}.turbine_kpi_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY record_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has total forecasted mwh trended over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT snapshot_date, MEASURE(total_forecasted_mwh) AS total_forecasted_mwh",
        "FROM {fqn}.wind_forecast_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY snapshot_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has total power purchase agreement price per mwh trended over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT snapshot_date, MEASURE(total_ppa_price_mwh) AS total_ppa_price_mwh",
        "FROM {fqn}.wind_forecast_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY snapshot_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "Which turbines have the highest total *?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT turbine_name, SUM(*) AS record_count, SUM(avg_wind_speed_ms) AS total_avg_wind_speed_ms",
        "FROM {fqn}.wind_turbines",
        "WHERE turbine_status = 'Fault'",
        "GROUP BY turbine_name",
        "ORDER BY total_avg_wind_speed_ms DESC",
        "LIMIT 10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the trend of total blade pitch angle in degrees over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT reading_date, SUM(blade_pitch_deg) AS total_blade_pitch_deg",
        "FROM {fqn}.performance_readings",
        "GROUP BY reading_date ORDER BY reading_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has average forecasted generation in mwh trended by month?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT snapshot_date, AVG(forecasted_generation_mwh) AS avg_forecasted_generation_mwh",
        "FROM {fqn}.wind_snapshots",
        "GROUP BY snapshot_date",
        "ORDER BY snapshot_date"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "sql_snippets": {
    "filters": [
      {
        "sql": "wind_turbines.turbine_status = 'Generating'",
        "display_name": "generating turbines",
        "synonyms": [
          "active turbines",
          "producing turbines"
        ],
        "instruction": "Use when filtering to actively generating wind turbines."
      },
      {
        "sql": "wind_turbines.turbine_status IN ('Fault', 'Maintenance')",
        "display_name": "turbines down",
        "synonyms": [
          "offline turbines",
          "unavailable turbines"
        ],
        "instruction": "Use when filtering to turbines in fault or maintenance."
      },
